{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CJ2", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-descent-lemma-smooth-local-source-target}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-descending-property-lci}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-lci-syntomic-local-source}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-local-source-target}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-section-lci}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fde286bbcc5c3b3f03e247c6ca4c3aa289afa1118f7013e38b025b1b48510024", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe property ``being a local complete intersection morphism''\nof morphisms of algebraic spaces is\nsmooth local on the source-and-target, see\nDescent on Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>\nand\nMore on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemmas\n<REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0004> above, we may define what it\nmeans for a morphism of algebraic spaces to be\na local complete intersection morphism as follows and it agrees with the\nalready existing notion defined in\nMore on Morphisms of Spaces,\nSection <REF_0005>\nwhen both source and target are algebraic spaces.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cd41069427a4bd3d5bd1929d9d1d02844f02756bb726b76458c1a0e71cf60c8f", "unit_id": "tag:0CJ2:prose-0001"}
